curacy. By conducting generalization tests on different sub-datasets, differences are identified between the original datasets in terms of topological types, chemical elements, unknown magnetic compounds, and feature space coverage. Their impact on model performance is analyzed.\nTurning to the simpler binary classification between trivial insulators and nontrivial topological materials, three different approaches are also tested. Key characteristics influencing material topology are identified, with the maximum packing efficiency and the fraction of p valence electrons being highlighted as critical features.","descriptionType":"Abstract"}],"geoLocations":[],"fundingReferences":[],"xml":"","url":"https://archive.materialscloud.org/doi/10.24435/materialscloud:m0-zg","contentUrl":null,"metadataVersion":2,"schemaVersion":"http://datacite.org/schema/kernel-4","source":"api","isActive":true,"state":"findable","reason":null,"viewCount":0,"viewsOverTime":[],"downloadCount":0,"downloadsOverTime":[],"referenceCount":0,"citationCount":1,"citationsOverTime":[{"year":"2026","total":2}],"partCount":0,"partOfCount":0,"versionCount":2,"versionOfCount":0,"created":"2025-06-24T11:11:47.000Z","registered":"2025-06-24T11:11:48.000Z","published":"2025","updated":"2026-11-02T13:29:02.000Z"},"relationships":{"client":{"data":{"id":"ethz.marvel","type":"clients"}},"provider":{"data":{"id":"hedk","type":"providers"}},"media":{"data":{"id":"10.24435/materialscloud:m0-zg","type":"media"}},"references":{"data":[]},"citations":{"data":[{"id":"10.1038/s41524-025-01687-2","type":"dois"}]},"parts":{"data":[]},"partOf":{"data":[]},"versions":{"data":[{"id":"10.24435/materialscloud:xx-xb","type":"dois"},{"id":"10.24435/materialscloud:zk-gc","type":"dois"}]},"versionOf":{"data":[]}}}}